From: OmacVM
Subject: [PATCH] ui: the VM's window takes the pointer without a click

What: the main view takes an absolute pointer (virtio-tablet) on the first
motion over it, and when its window becomes key, the app active, the window
full screen, the pointer mode absolute or the guest's pointer comes up,
whenever the pointer is on the VM's picture and nothing is above it
(ui/omacvm-pointer-start.h decides). The Mac's cursor over the VM is hidden
only once the guest draws its own pointer (show-cursor=off and Omarchy's
display agent said hello since the last guest reset), from one place, once.
OMACVM_POINTER_START=0 keeps upstream's way (on enter or a click; hidden
with every grab). The log says which ("cocoa: pointer: ...").

Why: after every VM start, and after a guest reboot, the guest's pointer
sat in the middle and did not move until the user clicked once into the
window (user, 2026-10-05 15:00). Upstream takes an absolute pointer only on
mouseEntered or a click. The window opens under the pointer, comes back key
with the pointer on it (OmacVM.app hands it the focus after a start; the
escape combo; Command-Tab), or loses the grab without the pointer moving (a
key change during the start, the guest's screen changing at a reboot):
nothing enters, so nothing took it. Full screen grabbed at once, before the
app was in front and while the guest still booted: the Mac's cursor was
hidden with no guest pointer drawn, and a second grab (full screen after a
click) hid it twice, so one let-go left it hidden.

Test hook (test mode only, OMACVM_TEST_SKIP_DISPLAYS): OMACVM_TEST_POINTER=
<seconds> sends made-up motion over the main view through mouseMoved: four
times a second from the start, as if the user moved the mouse and never
clicked; the window counts as key and in front, the full-screen guard is
skipped for it and the Mac's cursor is only logged (never the real one).
OMACVM_POINTER_DEBUG=1 logs each take and the cursor's state.

Upstream: not proposed (OmacVM's pointer policy and display agent).
Test: app/runtime/Tests/display/test-pointer-start.c (the decisions, with a
model of the view; also shows upstream's static pointer);
src/tests/pointer-start-vm.sh (a throwaway VM on a virtual display: the
guest gets motion right after the start and after a reboot, no click).

